Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: GRX500: classify module memory using the EVA direct map

The OpenWrt short-call module allocator distinguishes page/kmalloc allocations
from vmalloc using KSEG0. GRX500 EVA maps cached DDR at PAGE_OFFSET=0x60000000,
so both PLT cleanup and executable init-memory cleanup incorrectly call vfree
on direct-map addresses. Use the actual low-memory range for this platform.
The same predicate also selects the physical versus virtual PLT table.

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/module.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/module.c
@@ -206,7 +206,11 @@ static inline bool is_phys_addr(void *ptr)
 {
-#ifdef CONFIG_64BIT
+#if defined(CONFIG_SOC_GRX500) && defined(CONFIG_EVA)
+	/* EVA cached DDR is not in the conventional KSEG0 segment. */
+	return (unsigned long)ptr >= PAGE_OFFSET &&
+	       (unsigned long)ptr < (unsigned long)high_memory;
+#elif defined(CONFIG_64BIT)
 	return (KSEGX((unsigned long)ptr) == CKSEG0);
 #else
 	return (KSEGX(ptr) == KSEG0);
 #endif
 }
